[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186381049 :answer-field/choices 17592186381050] [:db/retract 17592186381049 :answer-field/choices 17592186381051] [:db/retract 17592186381049 :answer-field/choices 17592186381052] [:db/retract 17592186381049 :answer-field/choices 17592186381053] [:db/retract 17592186381049 :answer-field/choices 17592186381054] {:db/id 17592186157605 :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3}{4}(2x-{x}^{2}),\\,0\\le x\\le 2.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{3}].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the third raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}(2x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{4}-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{10}{x}^{5}-\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{6})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3\\cdot {2}^{5}}{10}-\\frac{{2}^{6}}{8})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{5}-8 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153874 :answer-field/correct 17592186153879 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129188 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7534ff45-14c3-5354-a5be-41324d6a8d58"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7534ff45-14c3-5354-a5be-41324d6a8d58" :question/id #uuid "7534ff45-14c3-5354-a5be-41324d6a8d58" :question/math-academy-id "q-81246" :question/problem "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=-7,\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=19,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}2f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}2f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =2{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =2(-7+19) \\\\  & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5f5a94fb-044e-5125-bc1a-367ebc8a739b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5f5a94fb-044e-5125-bc1a-367ebc8a739b" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f5a94fb-044e-5125-bc1a-367ebc8a739b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-08859865-52fe-5dbb-8f26-32959c6acbd7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-128be196-9e1b-5546-be5b-900e9b7b4df5" "answer-08859865-52fe-5dbb-8f26-32959c6acbd7" "answer-a86dd52e-3027-5c20-8506-094ac20452c7" "answer-adc94108-5e06-511a-9533-0be105c23e85" "answer-2862b1c1-f759-5410-aa00-ccf9a4520165"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-128be196-9e1b-5546-be5b-900e9b7b4df5" :answer/id #uuid "128be196-9e1b-5546-be5b-900e9b7b4df5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08859865-52fe-5dbb-8f26-32959c6acbd7" :answer/id #uuid "08859865-52fe-5dbb-8f26-32959c6acbd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a86dd52e-3027-5c20-8506-094ac20452c7" :answer/id #uuid "a86dd52e-3027-5c20-8506-094ac20452c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-adc94108-5e06-511a-9533-0be105c23e85" :answer/id #uuid "adc94108-5e06-511a-9533-0be105c23e85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2862b1c1-f759-5410-aa00-ccf9a4520165" :answer/id #uuid "2862b1c1-f759-5410-aa00-ccf9a4520165" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162062 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-59606949-3c87-521e-a2c2-60c040472354"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-59606949-3c87-521e-a2c2-60c040472354" :question/id #uuid "59606949-3c87-521e-a2c2-60c040472354" :question/math-academy-id "q-109956" :question/problem "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=16$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=6.$ Find $\\text{Var}[\\frac{3}{8}X+\\frac{1}{2}Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[\\frac{3}{8}X+\\frac{1}{2}Y]={(\\frac{3}{8})}^{2}\\cdot 16+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot 6=\\frac{15}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3a192929-90b9-5ade-b716-7719dbfc5bbf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3a192929-90b9-5ade-b716-7719dbfc5bbf" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a192929-90b9-5ade-b716-7719dbfc5bbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-074012c5-6ca1-5495-8009-0d0c255d3ee8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1bc800b9-5ce9-51df-9646-ad28b4b5f5dd" "answer-d18a0d10-9bd4-5e8e-9023-0b2590d9b92f" "answer-81f7e7be-4c3c-5db4-9e89-a897730e6bd7" "answer-074012c5-6ca1-5495-8009-0d0c255d3ee8" "answer-afc9329d-23eb-511f-aef5-7c8e3284646b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1bc800b9-5ce9-51df-9646-ad28b4b5f5dd" :answer/id #uuid "1bc800b9-5ce9-51df-9646-ad28b4b5f5dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d18a0d10-9bd4-5e8e-9023-0b2590d9b92f" :answer/id #uuid "d18a0d10-9bd4-5e8e-9023-0b2590d9b92f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81f7e7be-4c3c-5db4-9e89-a897730e6bd7" :answer/id #uuid "81f7e7be-4c3c-5db4-9e89-a897730e6bd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{155}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-074012c5-6ca1-5495-8009-0d0c255d3ee8" :answer/id #uuid "074012c5-6ca1-5495-8009-0d0c255d3ee8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afc9329d-23eb-511f-aef5-7c8e3284646b" :answer/id #uuid "afc9329d-23eb-511f-aef5-7c8e3284646b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{41}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186381048 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $f(x,y)=\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{y}$ is defined only when $y\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function ${f}_{x}(x,y)=-\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{y}$ is defined only when $y\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{x}}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}.\n$$\n\n- Similarly, the domain of ${f}_{y}$ is the same: \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partials of $f$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}} & =\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}\\cap \\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}\\cap \\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186381049 :answer-field/correct "answer-d41c428c-d04e-5f2e-a433-2206f490a862" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f0bf3fe3-986e-545e-b34a-605fe91bb5de" "answer-646b7d0d-81dc-553a-84a0-b0fc791fa343" "answer-3f1523c2-f133-58a1-bbf8-fd7a6928b953" "answer-0c87158e-2c98-5786-92c3-7401ac9880a4" "answer-d41c428c-d04e-5f2e-a433-2206f490a862"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0bf3fe3-986e-545e-b34a-605fe91bb5de" :answer/id #uuid "f0bf3fe3-986e-545e-b34a-605fe91bb5de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y>0\\,\\text{and}\\,x>0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-646b7d0d-81dc-553a-84a0-b0fc791fa343" :answer/id #uuid "646b7d0d-81dc-553a-84a0-b0fc791fa343" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y>0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f1523c2-f133-58a1-bbf8-fd7a6928b953" :answer/id #uuid "3f1523c2-f133-58a1-bbf8-fd7a6928b953" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ge 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c87158e-2c98-5786-92c3-7401ac9880a4" :answer/id #uuid "0c87158e-2c98-5786-92c3-7401ac9880a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\,\\text{and}\\,x\\ge 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d41c428c-d04e-5f2e-a433-2206f490a862" :answer/id #uuid "d41c428c-d04e-5f2e-a433-2206f490a862" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162588 :question/problem "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-{x}_{2}{y}_{3}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-{x}_{2}{y}_{3}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2-3+0-4 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186160820 :answer-field/correct 17592186160825 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162240 :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$  Given that the random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(10),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X>x)=0.950.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $8$ | $\\,1.344\\,$ | $\\,1.646\\,$ | $\\,2.180\\,$ | $\\,2.733\\,$ | $\\,3.490\\,$ |\n| $9$ | $\\,1.735\\,$ | $\\,2.088\\,$ | $\\,2.700\\,$ | $\\,3.325\\,$ | $\\,4.168\\,$ |\n| $10$ | $\\,2.156\\,$ | $\\,2.558\\,$ | $\\,3.247\\,$ | $\\,3.940\\,$ | $\\,4.865\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Since $X∼{χ}^{2}(10),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=10.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $10$ | $\\,2.156\\,$ | $\\,2.558\\,$ | $\\,3.247\\,$ | $\\,3.940\\,$ | $\\,4.865\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X>3.940)=0.950.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=3.940.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186158642 :answer-field/correct 17592186158644 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b555139b-2962-5dd6-b346-b8e6df95cc7b" :activity/id #uuid "b555139b-2962-5dd6-b346-b8e6df95cc7b" :activity/title "Quiz 10" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-0227aae6-d172-57f4-83e8-b1350d2428e9" "step-e89dc435-8fab-54ad-b411-67e8259e3a52" "step-35856cad-af45-592b-875b-efaabf6558c1" "step-377d1b56-e249-5637-8fc7-52e7cdfb6112" "step-baf61fcf-e594-5cc6-83eb-990554bce235" "step-b888148b-c958-5b54-a1f1-35cce9975a68" "step-818eca0c-b233-5882-9188-be81b881f643" "step-8a77be89-756b-53de-80cd-2a432d18bca3"] :activity/first-step "step-0227aae6-d172-57f4-83e8-b1350d2428e9" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-0227aae6-d172-57f4-83e8-b1350d2428e9" :step/id #uuid "0227aae6-d172-57f4-83e8-b1350d2428e9" :step/content 17592186157605 :step/next "step-e89dc435-8fab-54ad-b411-67e8259e3a52" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e89dc435-8fab-54ad-b411-67e8259e3a52" :step/id #uuid "e89dc435-8fab-54ad-b411-67e8259e3a52" :step/content "question-7534ff45-14c3-5354-a5be-41324d6a8d58" :step/next "step-35856cad-af45-592b-875b-efaabf6558c1" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-35856cad-af45-592b-875b-efaabf6558c1" :step/id #uuid "35856cad-af45-592b-875b-efaabf6558c1" :step/content "question-59606949-3c87-521e-a2c2-60c040472354" :step/next "step-377d1b56-e249-5637-8fc7-52e7cdfb6112" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-377d1b56-e249-5637-8fc7-52e7cdfb6112" :step/id #uuid "377d1b56-e249-5637-8fc7-52e7cdfb6112" :step/content 17592186272239 :step/next "step-baf61fcf-e594-5cc6-83eb-990554bce235" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-baf61fcf-e594-5cc6-83eb-990554bce235" :step/id #uuid "baf61fcf-e594-5cc6-83eb-990554bce235" :step/content 17592186326849 :step/next "step-b888148b-c958-5b54-a1f1-35cce9975a68" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b888148b-c958-5b54-a1f1-35cce9975a68" :step/id #uuid "b888148b-c958-5b54-a1f1-35cce9975a68" :step/content 17592186381048 :step/next "step-818eca0c-b233-5882-9188-be81b881f643" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-818eca0c-b233-5882-9188-be81b881f643" :step/id #uuid "818eca0c-b233-5882-9188-be81b881f643" :step/content 17592186162588 :step/next "step-8a77be89-756b-53de-80cd-2a432d18bca3" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8a77be89-756b-53de-80cd-2a432d18bca3" :step/id #uuid "8a77be89-756b-53de-80cd-2a432d18bca3" :step/content 17592186162240 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186157605 :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3}{4}(2x-{x}^{2}),\\,0\\le x\\le 2.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{3}].$"] [17592186157605 :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the third raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}(2x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{4}-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{10}{x}^{5}-\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{6})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3\\cdot {2}^{5}}{10}-\\frac{{2}^{6}}{8})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{5}-8 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186157605 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186153874 :answer-field/correct 17592186153879] ["question-7534ff45-14c3-5354-a5be-41324d6a8d58" :question/id #uuid "7534ff45-14c3-5354-a5be-41324d6a8d58"] ["question-7534ff45-14c3-5354-a5be-41324d6a8d58" :question/math-academy-id "q-81246"] ["question-7534ff45-14c3-5354-a5be-41324d6a8d58" :question/problem "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=-7,\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=19,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}2f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$"] ["question-7534ff45-14c3-5354-a5be-41324d6a8d58" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}2f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =2{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =2(-7+19) \\\\  & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-7534ff45-14c3-5354-a5be-41324d6a8d58" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-5f5a94fb-044e-5125-bc1a-367ebc8a739b" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f5a94fb-044e-5125-bc1a-367ebc8a739b"] ["answer-128be196-9e1b-5546-be5b-900e9b7b4df5" :answer/id #uuid "128be196-9e1b-5546-be5b-900e9b7b4df5"] ["answer-128be196-9e1b-5546-be5b-900e9b7b4df5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-128be196-9e1b-5546-be5b-900e9b7b4df5" :answer/value "12"] ["answer-08859865-52fe-5dbb-8f26-32959c6acbd7" :answer/id #uuid "08859865-52fe-5dbb-8f26-32959c6acbd7"] ["answer-08859865-52fe-5dbb-8f26-32959c6acbd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-08859865-52fe-5dbb-8f26-32959c6acbd7" :answer/value "24"] ["answer-a86dd52e-3027-5c20-8506-094ac20452c7" :answer/id #uuid "a86dd52e-3027-5c20-8506-094ac20452c7"] ["answer-a86dd52e-3027-5c20-8506-094ac20452c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a86dd52e-3027-5c20-8506-094ac20452c7" :answer/value "36"] ["answer-adc94108-5e06-511a-9533-0be105c23e85" :answer/id #uuid "adc94108-5e06-511a-9533-0be105c23e85"] ["answer-adc94108-5e06-511a-9533-0be105c23e85" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-adc94108-5e06-511a-9533-0be105c23e85" :answer/value "48"] ["answer-2862b1c1-f759-5410-aa00-ccf9a4520165" :answer/id #uuid "2862b1c1-f759-5410-aa00-ccf9a4520165"] ["answer-2862b1c1-f759-5410-aa00-ccf9a4520165" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2862b1c1-f759-5410-aa00-ccf9a4520165" :answer/value "60"] ["answer-field-5f5a94fb-044e-5125-bc1a-367ebc8a739b" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-5f5a94fb-044e-5125-bc1a-367ebc8a739b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-5f5a94fb-044e-5125-bc1a-367ebc8a739b" :answer-field/correct "answer-08859865-52fe-5dbb-8f26-32959c6acbd7"] ["answer-field-5f5a94fb-044e-5125-bc1a-367ebc8a739b" :answer-field/choices "answer-128be196-9e1b-5546-be5b-900e9b7b4df5"] ["answer-field-5f5a94fb-044e-5125-bc1a-367ebc8a739b" :answer-field/choices "answer-08859865-52fe-5dbb-8f26-32959c6acbd7"] ["answer-field-5f5a94fb-044e-5125-bc1a-367ebc8a739b" :answer-field/choices "answer-a86dd52e-3027-5c20-8506-094ac20452c7"] ["answer-field-5f5a94fb-044e-5125-bc1a-367ebc8a739b" :answer-field/choices "answer-adc94108-5e06-511a-9533-0be105c23e85"] ["answer-field-5f5a94fb-044e-5125-bc1a-367ebc8a739b" :answer-field/choices "answer-2862b1c1-f759-5410-aa00-ccf9a4520165"] ["question-7534ff45-14c3-5354-a5be-41324d6a8d58" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-5f5a94fb-044e-5125-bc1a-367ebc8a739b"] [17592186129188 :knowledge-point/questions "question-7534ff45-14c3-5354-a5be-41324d6a8d58"] ["question-59606949-3c87-521e-a2c2-60c040472354" :question/id #uuid "59606949-3c87-521e-a2c2-60c040472354"] ["question-59606949-3c87-521e-a2c2-60c040472354" :question/math-academy-id "q-109956"] ["question-59606949-3c87-521e-a2c2-60c040472354" :question/problem "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=16$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=6.$ Find $\\text{Var}[\\frac{3}{8}X+\\frac{1}{2}Y].$"] ["question-59606949-3c87-521e-a2c2-60c040472354" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[\\frac{3}{8}X+\\frac{1}{2}Y]={(\\frac{3}{8})}^{2}\\cdot 16+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot 6=\\frac{15}{4}.\n$$"] ["question-59606949-3c87-521e-a2c2-60c040472354" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-3a192929-90b9-5ade-b716-7719dbfc5bbf" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a192929-90b9-5ade-b716-7719dbfc5bbf"] ["answer-1bc800b9-5ce9-51df-9646-ad28b4b5f5dd" :answer/id #uuid "1bc800b9-5ce9-51df-9646-ad28b4b5f5dd"] ["answer-1bc800b9-5ce9-51df-9646-ad28b4b5f5dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1bc800b9-5ce9-51df-9646-ad28b4b5f5dd" :answer/value "6"] ["answer-d18a0d10-9bd4-5e8e-9023-0b2590d9b92f" :answer/id #uuid "d18a0d10-9bd4-5e8e-9023-0b2590d9b92f"] ["answer-d18a0d10-9bd4-5e8e-9023-0b2590d9b92f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d18a0d10-9bd4-5e8e-9023-0b2590d9b92f" :answer/value "9"] ["answer-81f7e7be-4c3c-5db4-9e89-a897730e6bd7" :answer/id #uuid "81f7e7be-4c3c-5db4-9e89-a897730e6bd7"] ["answer-81f7e7be-4c3c-5db4-9e89-a897730e6bd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-81f7e7be-4c3c-5db4-9e89-a897730e6bd7" :answer/value "\\frac{155}{32}"] ["answer-074012c5-6ca1-5495-8009-0d0c255d3ee8" :answer/id #uuid "074012c5-6ca1-5495-8009-0d0c255d3ee8"] ["answer-074012c5-6ca1-5495-8009-0d0c255d3ee8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-074012c5-6ca1-5495-8009-0d0c255d3ee8" :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}"] ["answer-afc9329d-23eb-511f-aef5-7c8e3284646b" :answer/id #uuid "afc9329d-23eb-511f-aef5-7c8e3284646b"] ["answer-afc9329d-23eb-511f-aef5-7c8e3284646b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-afc9329d-23eb-511f-aef5-7c8e3284646b" :answer/value "\\frac{41}{4}"] ["answer-field-3a192929-90b9-5ade-b716-7719dbfc5bbf" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-3a192929-90b9-5ade-b716-7719dbfc5bbf" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-3a192929-90b9-5ade-b716-7719dbfc5bbf" :answer-field/correct "answer-074012c5-6ca1-5495-8009-0d0c255d3ee8"] ["answer-field-3a192929-90b9-5ade-b716-7719dbfc5bbf" :answer-field/choices "answer-1bc800b9-5ce9-51df-9646-ad28b4b5f5dd"] ["answer-field-3a192929-90b9-5ade-b716-7719dbfc5bbf" :answer-field/choices "answer-d18a0d10-9bd4-5e8e-9023-0b2590d9b92f"] ["answer-field-3a192929-90b9-5ade-b716-7719dbfc5bbf" :answer-field/choices "answer-81f7e7be-4c3c-5db4-9e89-a897730e6bd7"] ["answer-field-3a192929-90b9-5ade-b716-7719dbfc5bbf" :answer-field/choices "answer-074012c5-6ca1-5495-8009-0d0c255d3ee8"] ["answer-field-3a192929-90b9-5ade-b716-7719dbfc5bbf" :answer-field/choices "answer-afc9329d-23eb-511f-aef5-7c8e3284646b"] ["question-59606949-3c87-521e-a2c2-60c040472354" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-3a192929-90b9-5ade-b716-7719dbfc5bbf"] [17592186162062 :knowledge-point/questions "question-59606949-3c87-521e-a2c2-60c040472354"] [17592186381048 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $f(x,y)=\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{y}$ is defined only when $y\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function ${f}_{x}(x,y)=-\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{y}$ is defined only when $y\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{x}}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}.\n$$\n\n- Similarly, the domain of ${f}_{y}$ is the same: \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partials of $f$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}} & =\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}\\cap \\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}\\cap \\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["answer-f0bf3fe3-986e-545e-b34a-605fe91bb5de" :answer/id #uuid "f0bf3fe3-986e-545e-b34a-605fe91bb5de"] ["answer-f0bf3fe3-986e-545e-b34a-605fe91bb5de" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f0bf3fe3-986e-545e-b34a-605fe91bb5de" :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y>0\\,\\text{and}\\,x>0\\}"] ["answer-646b7d0d-81dc-553a-84a0-b0fc791fa343" :answer/id #uuid "646b7d0d-81dc-553a-84a0-b0fc791fa343"] ["answer-646b7d0d-81dc-553a-84a0-b0fc791fa343" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-646b7d0d-81dc-553a-84a0-b0fc791fa343" :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y>0\\}"] ["answer-3f1523c2-f133-58a1-bbf8-fd7a6928b953" :answer/id #uuid "3f1523c2-f133-58a1-bbf8-fd7a6928b953"] ["answer-3f1523c2-f133-58a1-bbf8-fd7a6928b953" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3f1523c2-f133-58a1-bbf8-fd7a6928b953" :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ge 0\\}"] ["answer-0c87158e-2c98-5786-92c3-7401ac9880a4" :answer/id #uuid "0c87158e-2c98-5786-92c3-7401ac9880a4"] ["answer-0c87158e-2c98-5786-92c3-7401ac9880a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0c87158e-2c98-5786-92c3-7401ac9880a4" :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\,\\text{and}\\,x\\ge 0\\}"] ["answer-d41c428c-d04e-5f2e-a433-2206f490a862" :answer/id #uuid "d41c428c-d04e-5f2e-a433-2206f490a862"] ["answer-d41c428c-d04e-5f2e-a433-2206f490a862" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d41c428c-d04e-5f2e-a433-2206f490a862" :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}"] [17592186381049 :answer-field/correct "answer-d41c428c-d04e-5f2e-a433-2206f490a862"] [17592186381049 :answer-field/choices "answer-f0bf3fe3-986e-545e-b34a-605fe91bb5de"] [17592186381049 :answer-field/choices "answer-646b7d0d-81dc-553a-84a0-b0fc791fa343"] [17592186381049 :answer-field/choices "answer-3f1523c2-f133-58a1-bbf8-fd7a6928b953"] [17592186381049 :answer-field/choices "answer-0c87158e-2c98-5786-92c3-7401ac9880a4"] [17592186381049 :answer-field/choices "answer-d41c428c-d04e-5f2e-a433-2206f490a862"] [17592186162588 :question/problem "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-{x}_{2}{y}_{3}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$"] [17592186162588 :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-{x}_{2}{y}_{3}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2-3+0-4 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186162588 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [17592186160820 :answer-field/correct 17592186160825] [17592186162240 :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$  Given that the random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(10),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X>x)=0.950.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $8$ | $\\,1.344\\,$ | $\\,1.646\\,$ | $\\,2.180\\,$ | $\\,2.733\\,$ | $\\,3.490\\,$ |\n| $9$ | $\\,1.735\\,$ | $\\,2.088\\,$ | $\\,2.700\\,$ | $\\,3.325\\,$ | $\\,4.168\\,$ |\n| $10$ | $\\,2.156\\,$ | $\\,2.558\\,$ | $\\,3.247\\,$ | $\\,3.940\\,$ | $\\,4.865\\,$ |"] [17592186162240 :question/worked-solution "Since $X∼{χ}^{2}(10),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=10.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $10$ | $\\,2.156\\,$ | $\\,2.558\\,$ | $\\,3.247\\,$ | $\\,3.940\\,$ | $\\,4.865\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X>3.940)=0.950.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=3.940.$"] [17592186162240 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [17592186158642 :answer-field/correct 17592186158644] ["activity-b555139b-2962-5dd6-b346-b8e6df95cc7b" :activity/id #uuid "b555139b-2962-5dd6-b346-b8e6df95cc7b"] ["step-0227aae6-d172-57f4-83e8-b1350d2428e9" :step/id #uuid "0227aae6-d172-57f4-83e8-b1350d2428e9"] ["step-e89dc435-8fab-54ad-b411-67e8259e3a52" :step/id #uuid "e89dc435-8fab-54ad-b411-67e8259e3a52"] ["step-35856cad-af45-592b-875b-efaabf6558c1" :step/id #uuid "35856cad-af45-592b-875b-efaabf6558c1"] ["step-377d1b56-e249-5637-8fc7-52e7cdfb6112" :step/id #uuid "377d1b56-e249-5637-8fc7-52e7cdfb6112"] ["step-baf61fcf-e594-5cc6-83eb-990554bce235" :step/id #uuid "baf61fcf-e594-5cc6-83eb-990554bce235"] ["step-b888148b-c958-5b54-a1f1-35cce9975a68" :step/id #uuid "b888148b-c958-5b54-a1f1-35cce9975a68"] ["step-818eca0c-b233-5882-9188-be81b881f643" :step/id #uuid "818eca0c-b233-5882-9188-be81b881f643"] ["step-8a77be89-756b-53de-80cd-2a432d18bca3" :step/id #uuid "8a77be89-756b-53de-80cd-2a432d18bca3"] ["step-0227aae6-d172-57f4-83e8-b1350d2428e9" :step/content 17592186157605] ["step-0227aae6-d172-57f4-83e8-b1350d2428e9" :step/next "step-e89dc435-8fab-54ad-b411-67e8259e3a52"] ["step-e89dc435-8fab-54ad-b411-67e8259e3a52" :step/content "question-7534ff45-14c3-5354-a5be-41324d6a8d58"] ["step-e89dc435-8fab-54ad-b411-67e8259e3a52" :step/next "step-35856cad-af45-592b-875b-efaabf6558c1"] ["step-35856cad-af45-592b-875b-efaabf6558c1" :step/content "question-59606949-3c87-521e-a2c2-60c040472354"] ["step-35856cad-af45-592b-875b-efaabf6558c1" :step/next "step-377d1b56-e249-5637-8fc7-52e7cdfb6112"] ["step-377d1b56-e249-5637-8fc7-52e7cdfb6112" :step/content 17592186272239] ["