ontinuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$f(x) = \\frac{3}{4}(2x - x^{2}), 0 \\le x \\le 2$.\n\nCalculate $E[X^{3}]$."] [17592186381048 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $f(x,y)=\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{y}$ is defined only when $y\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}={(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function ${f}_{x}(x,y)=-\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{y}$ is defined only when $y\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{x}}={(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\n- Similarly, the domain of ${f}_{y}$ is the same: \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}={(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partials of $f$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}} & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0}\\cap {(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0}\\cap {(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0} \\\\  & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186381049 :answer-field/correct 17592186381053] [17592186381049 :answer-field/choices 17592186381050] [17592186381049 :answer-field/choices 17592186381051] [17592186381049 :answer-field/choices 17592186381052] [17592186381049 :answer-field/choices 17592186381053] [17592186381049 :answer-field/choices 17592186381054] [17592186162588 :question/problem "Consider the bilinear form $B(x, y)$, given by\n\n$B(x, y) = x_{1}y_{1} - 3x_{1}y_{3} - x_{2}y_{3} + x_{3}y_{3}$.\n\nEvaluate $B(x, y)$ when $x = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $y = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186162240 :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X \\ge x) = p$, where $X∼χ^{2}(k)$. Given that the random variable $X∼χ^{2}(10)$, find the value of $x$ such that $P(X > x) = 0.950$.\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $8$ | $1.344$ | $1.646$ | $2.180$ | $2.733$ | $3.490$ |\n| $9$ | $1.735$ | $2.088$ | $2.700$ | $3.325$ | $4.168$ |\n| $10